    {
      "id": "stk-p1039886-gs321",
      "uid": "stk-mohammy",
      "code": "GS 321",
      "sec": "srcU",
      "ts": 1337439174000,
      "st": "pub",
      "data": {
        "html": "يا شباب شكلكم مضيعين. انا منزل مع جارس و عطانا ورقة فيها اسألة و الإختبار مب يجي الا منها حسب كلامه. الاسألة تقدرون تقولون شاملة لمتيريال الإختبار بس تخليك تعرف شتذاكر بالضبط.<br><br>هذي الأسألة:<br><br>Health Psychology<br><br>What is stress? What causes it?<br><br>Describe the three categories of stressors (including examples).<br><br>Can stress be beneficial? Explain.<br><br>What are the different categories of coping strategies? Which strategies are ineffective, and why?<br><br>Describe the effect of personality and stress on heart disease.<br><br>What predicts happiness/well-being? What doesn’t?<br><br>Define and explain the General Adaptation Syndrome.<br><br>Social Psychology<br><br>Explain the impression formation process. What role do schemas play?<br><br>What are the two main types of attributions? State and explain the two main errors in attribution.<br><br>What are the main compliance techniques described in the book? Why are they effective?<br><br>Know and be able to differentiate between stereotypes, prejudice, and discrimination.<br><br>What factors contribute to attraction/liking? How?<br><br>What are the three components to consider in persuasion? What role does processing play?<br><br>Compare and contrast the three main types of Social Influence.<br><br>When does aggression and helping behavior occur?<br><br>Thinking<br><br>What are schemas and prototypes? How do we use them?<br><br>Distinguish between Algorithms and Heuristics and know when each are used.<br><br>What is fixedness and what role does it play in problem solving?<br><br>How is creativity important (including its relation to convergent and divergent thinking) in problem solving?<br><br>What is the process of problem solving? What problems can occur? What be helpful?<br><br>What are the different approaches to intelligence? Compare the traditional, single-factor approach to intelligence to newer approaches.<br><br>How is intelligence measured? How do the tests differ?<br><br>Personality<br><br>What is personality? What effect does it have on behavior and thinking?<br><br>Describe the main approaches to personality and identify the strengths and weakness of each.<br><br>List and describe the Big Five personality traits.<br><br>What’s the difference between self-esteem and self-efficacy?<br><br>List and describe the three main components of personality, according to Freud. How do they interact?<br><br>What are defense mechanisms? Why/when are they used?<br><br>Describe the main methods of assessing personality?<br><br>Memory<br><br>What are encoding, storage, and retrieval? How do they work together?<br><br>Describe the three types/stages of memory (including their limitations) and describe how they interact.<br><br>What role does encoding play in the memory process? How does chunking and repetition aid the encoding process?<br><br>What are the different kinds of retrieval and how do they work? Why might retrieval fail?<br><br>What are explicit and implicit memory? How do they differ?<br><br>What are the different types of forgetting? When do they occur?<br><br>​<span data-fid=\"stk-f1039886-0\" class=\"src-fchip\" contenteditable=\"false\"></span>​",
